F. Roller lead s, default tube: rms of the varying radial error (median over phases), and the fraction of the shape it leaves. The lead costs 2 sin(n s / 2R) of harmonic n.
   s (mm)   lead angle   n=1     n=2     n=3     n=4    rms med   [gain 2 sin(n s / 2R)]
      0       0.0 deg   0.00    0.00    0.00    0.00     0.000
      4       3.7 deg   0.06    0.13    0.19    0.26     0.011
      6       5.6 deg   0.10    0.19    0.29    0.39     0.017
     10       9.3 deg   0.16    0.32    0.48    0.64     0.028
     14      13.0 deg   0.23    0.45    0.67    0.87     0.039
     18      16.7 deg   0.29    0.57    0.85    1.10     0.050
     25      23.2 deg   0.40    0.79    1.14    1.45     0.068
     40      37.1 deg   0.64    1.21    1.65    1.92     0.103
   A lead does not have to stay: software with an actuator can delay the reading by s / v (2.1 s at 17 mm and 8 mm/s); a passive clip cannot.

G. The crown's radial win over a room-fixed gun on an indicated tube = w - (what the seat passes). Median rms difference room minus OD ring, mm (positive: the crown wins)
   rows: w (residual after indicating); columns: b2 (ovality) with k = 3 pads / k = 4 pads; b1 = 0.08, b3 = 0.03.
   The rig accepts a tube when the OD indicator reads <= 0.25 TIR, so accepted tubes have w + ovality + ... <= about 0.125 in amplitude: the corner cells
   (w = 0.125 with b2 = 0.11) are outside what the rig would accept and are kept only to show the trend.
   w = 0.0125   b2 = 0.03:  -0.002 / -0.000    b2 = 0.06:  -0.009 / -0.000    b2 = 0.11:  -0.027 / -0.000
   w = 0.0300   b2 = 0.03:   0.002 /  0.004    b2 = 0.06:  -0.006 /  0.003    b2 = 0.11:  -0.024 /  0.003
   w = 0.0600   b2 = 0.03:   0.012 /  0.015    b2 = 0.06:   0.004 /  0.013    b2 = 0.11:  -0.016 /  0.010
   w = 0.1250   b2 = 0.03:   0.046 /  0.048    b2 = 0.06:   0.035 /  0.045    b2 = 0.11:   0.010 /  0.037
   b1 (wall eccentricity) is common to the room-fixed gun and to every OD ring, so it raises the floor of both and cannot cancel the crown's win;
   what decides the radial win is w (how well the tube was indicated) against what the pads pass (ovality at k = 3, three-lobing at k = 4).
